    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Now the fight has moved to an even more valuable chip. Nvidias AI processors are the most wanted technology on the planet. They train artificial intelligence, run giant data centers, and could power the next generation of weapons. Washington restricts which ones can go to China and Russia. Just this month, records released by a congressional committee showed US officials had approved sales of nearly nine hundred thousand advanced AI chips to China in only six months, and Congress is now fighting over whether that was a mistake. But the same playbook keeps showing up. In Singapore, prosecutors charged men over server deals worth hundreds of millions of dollars, accused of lying about where the machines would end up. American prosecutors charged a California businessman over roughly three hundred million dollars in Nvidia-powered servers, allegedly routed through Malaysia and Singapore to China. And one research firm found a Chinese reseller advertising eighty of Nvidias newest servers, stored in Malaysia, for shipment through Hong, Kong to Russia. Nobody has shown that sale ever happened. But the offer alone tells you the market is there.",
